<title>UK: Klesh&amp;Co says may have looked at Olivetti.</title>
<headline>Klesh&amp;Co says may have looked at Olivetti.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK-based Klesch and Co, which specialises in defaulted corporate debt, said on Friday it may have looked at stricken Italian information technology group Olivetti but declined to confirm it was considering a bid.</p>
<p>&quot;It would be not surprising if we had looked at various parts of Olivetti. But I'm not confirming that we have looked at various parts,&quot; Jeff Summers, head of research at Klesch and Co, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Klesh and Co, run by U.S. corporate debt trader Gary Klesch, has been tipped by Italian financial daily Il Sole as a bidder for Olivetti's troubled personal computer subsidiary.</p>
